mcrelay (1.2~beta11-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * New upstream release: bounded long-lived worker resource usage and
    relay timeouts, hardened configuration and protocol handling, and
    DNS responses bound to their queries.
  * Breaking change: the configured log file itself must not be a symbolic
    link; use logrotate's rename/create workflow to rotate it instead.

 -- Bilin Tsui <bilintsui@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:37:54 +0800

mcrelay (1.2~beta10-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix a remotely triggerable stack buffer overflow when a rewritten
    modern LOGIN handshake outgrew the worker buffer; packet_write now
    enforces destination capacity and field limits, and rewrite
    failures close the connection instead of forwarding the original
    handshake.

 -- Bilin Tsui <bilintsui@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:17:23 +0800

mcrelay (1.2~beta9-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * New upstream release: listener-owned DNS resolution, bounded route
    preparation, and listener-relayed status connections.
  * Breaking configuration changes: require a numeric listen address and
    remove the obsolete netpriority options.

 -- Bilin Tsui <bilintsui@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:12:11 +0800

